  "creator": "CrossFit",
  "description": "A chipper of ten movements, 50 reps each, done in order for time: box jumps, jumping pull-ups, kettlebell swings, walking lunges, knees-to-elbows, push presses, back extensions, wall balls, burpees and double-unders. First posted in June 2005, it is the archetype of the long CrossFit grind; good times are under 20 minutes. The \"Dirty Thirty\" (30 reps each) is the standard scale.",
